                <pb facs="1175" n="1079" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1079"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Woodford to Mr.
                            Sherman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-04-16"><hi rendition="#italic">April 16,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 226.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am this morning in receipt of telegram
                    from Mr. Bartleman, United States consul at Malaga, Spain, stating that his
                    residence was stoned last evening. I have at once asked the Spanish Government
                    to protect all United States consuls and consular offices throughout Spain.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stewart L. Woodford</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
